# L §5.5: "round(x, u, a) ... may take it as the mode when every option is a rounding code (§2.2)".
# round(2.5, 1, down) = 2, round(2.5, 1, half-up) = 3 (L §7.2).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

axis rm
  down "rounds down"
  half-up "rounds half up"

input x: num
input one: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-01-01
  x = 2.5
  one = 1

ask q1: round(x, one, rm)
=== expect
q1 [rm = down]: 2
  reading: rm = down
  cut 2016-03-01
q1 [rm = half-up]: 3
  reading: rm = half-up
  cut 2016-03-01
